{"name":"Smoke Tree","hex":"#bb5f34","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"smoke tree","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common garden shrub of genus Cotinus.","Psorothamnus spinosus, a spiny tree of the American desert."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/smoke_tree"}],"entries":[{"title":"Smoke tree","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke tree, or smoketree, may refer to any of several plants, some of whose parts are finely divided and give the appearance of smoke from a distance:"},{"items":["Cotinus, a genus of garden shrub commonly referred to as smoketrees.\nCotinus coggygria, the European or Eurasian smoketree\nCotinus obovatus, the American smoketree","Cotinus coggygria, the European or Eurasian smoketree","Cotinus obovatus, the American smoketree","Psorothamnus spinosus, a legume tree of the American Mojave desert commonly referred to as the smoketree. In the spring it has vibrant purple blooms.","Euphorbia cotinifolia, or tropical smoketree"]},{"items":["Cotinus coggygria, the European or Eurasian smoketree","Cotinus obovatus, the American smoketree"]}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Smoke_tree_in_Autumn.jpg/330px-Smoke_tree_in_Autumn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke_tree"},{"title":"Smoke","blocks":[{"text":"Smoke is an aerosol emitted when a material undergoes combustion or pyrolysis, together with the quantity of air that is entrained or otherwise mixed into the mass. It is commonly an unwanted by-product of fires, but may also be used for pest control (fumigation), communication, defensive and offensive capabilities in the military, cooking, or smoking. It is used in rituals where incense, sage, or resin is burned to produce a smell for spiritual or magical purposes. It can also be a flavoring agent and preservative."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg/330px-Ognisko_ubt_0126.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smoke"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg/500px-Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg/500px-Smoke_chemical_composition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chemical composition distribution of volatile organic compounds released in smoke from a variety of solid fuels[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASmoke_chemical_composition.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg/330px-Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Diesel-smoke.jpg/330px-Diesel-smoke.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Emission of soot in the fumes of a large diesel truck, without particle filters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADiesel-smoke.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thum